[gd_scene load_steps=4 format=3 uid="uid://unitdirshadowfade"]

; A DirectionalLight3D's distance fade, and nothing else: seven equal posts run away from the view,
; and the orthogonal sun's short `directional_shadow_max_distance` ends its shadow part-way along the
; row. Godot fades the shadow out from `directional_shadow_fade_start` of that distance to the
; distance and draws none past it, so the near posts cast and the far ones do not. Every other shadow
; golden keeps its casters well inside the default 100-unit range, where the fade never reaches, so
; a shadow drawn past the range, or cut off without the fade, is invisible there.

